    "description": "Create or OVERWRITE the value of one existing key in one locale (it cannot create new keys; use push_file on the source locale for that). Pass \`value\` for a simple key, or \`plural_forms\` (CLDR category map, e.g. {"one": "...", "other": "..."}) for a plural key. Send exactly one of the two. A JSON project has no plural FORMS: an ICU plural or select there is ONE string, so send it as \`value\` with its selectors and argument names verbatim (e.g. {count, plural, one {# item} other {# items}}). \`plural_forms\` is for a key the project stores as separate forms (is_plural true, as gettext or Android do); splitting an ICU message into it writes a row the format cannot represent. The write is recorded as a human edit (state human_edited) and versioned server-side, so it wins over future AI batches. Overwriting the SOURCE locale marks targets stale and, if the project has auto-translate on, queues a background AI batch (spends AI word quota; its id is not returned, so check list_batches). Optional \`reviewer\` attributes the edit. Returns the fresh row. Requires the "write" ability.",
