  {
    "annotations": {
      "destructiveHint": true,
      "openWorldHint": false,
      "readOnlyHint": false,
    },
    "description": "Import a localization file into one locale; pass the file content as a string (max 10 MB before JSON escaping, which can enlarge it, so a file with many non-ASCII characters may be refused below 10 MB). Formats: json_flat, json_nested, android_xml, ios_strings, ios_stringsdict, flutter_arb, laravel_php, laravel_json, xliff_12, ios_xcstrings, gettext_po, yaml, csv, xlsx, xliff_20, java_properties, resx, markdown, unity_csv, unreal_po. Pushing the SOURCE locale creates new keys and updates source values; pushing a target locale writes translations for existing keys (unknown keys are reported, never created). Values are written as human edits, but the server keeps existing human edits over pushed values and reports them as conflicts. Mode "sync_removals" (source locale only) additionally DELETES every project key missing from the file. This is destructive; the default "merge" never deletes. When the project has auto-translate on, a push may queue an AI batch (returned in \`batch\`, quota permitting; see quota_exceeded, and translation_paused for any other stop on AI spend). Optional \`metadata\` (source locale only, and not for formats that carry descriptions in the file) is a JSON sidecar of key descriptions and length ceilings keyed by key name, e.g. {"cart.title": {"description": "Cart page heading", "max_length": 40}}; null clears a field, an absent field is left alone. The result then carries a \`metadata\` block, and a warning if the server ignored the sidecar. Requires the "push" ability.",
